hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16494","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabira, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you sniff water, exaggerate, unless you are fasting."
"16495","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hashim Isma'il ibn Kathir, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabira, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: When you perform ablution, run through the fingers."
"16496","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hashim Isma'il ibn Kathir, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabira, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he slaughtered for us a sheep, and said: Do not think, and he did not say: Let him not think, that we slaughtered it only for you, but we have sheep, so when it reaches a hundred we slaughter a sheep."
"16497","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Isma'il ibn Kathir Abu Hashim, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabira, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: When you perform ablution, exaggerate in sniffing water, so long as you are not fasting."
"16498","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Kathir Abu Hashim al-Makki narrated to us, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabira, from his father, delegate of Banu al-Muntafiq, he said: I set out, I and a companion of mine, until we reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we did not find him. So A'isha fed us dates and made porridge for us. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came walking briskly and said: Were you fed anything. We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. And while we were so, the shepherd drove the sheep into the enclosure with a kid in his hand. He said: Did it give birth. He said: Yes. He said: Then slaughter for us a sheep. Then he turned to us and said: Do not think, and he did not say: Let him not think, that we slaughtered the sheep for your sake. We have a hundred sheep, we do not want it to increase over it. So when the shepherd delivers a young, we order him to slaughter a sheep. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about ablution. He said: When you perform ablution, perfect it, and run through the fingers, and when you blow your nose, exaggerate, unless you are fasting. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife, and he mentioned her long tongue and her harm. So he said: Divorce her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, she has companionship and a child. He said: Then keep her, and command her. If there is good in her, she will do, and do not beat your wife as you beat your slave girl."
